 Hans Johnson drives a Brougham circuit in 1904, in Full or Balanced detail. Walk up and use the shared Interact control to Stop or Continue; Step back checks visitor clearance. Driver picks and Find use the named person and the vehicle’s current position. Light retires the occupied assembly.\n\nInspector retains the requested person through its first mount/shown redraw, while Back clears the pending selection. The portable drivers, horses, fitted hitch and reconstructed routes keep their provenance.\n\nMobile memory fixes preserve scenery and quality settings: avoid importing unsupported town scenes, use exact count-only flora/timber storage, and release or reconstruct static railway CPU data without changing the decoded geometry or colors. Memory ceilings are unchanged.\n\nValidation on pushed commit `1b1db388e4965a852f660a4fda2b5f467a97b907`:\n\n- All four native parts passed: 1,150 checks including 400 self-tests; each part stayed within its original 600-second limit.\n- Five actual-commit changelog/history/identifier checks and whitespace passed.\n- Matching Chromium 141 mobile memory passed: 1812 **224.63 MiB / 225**, 1904 **399.69 MiB / 400**.\n- Native paired GPU controls preserve flora output and 48 timber material/depth/shadow comparisons bit for bit. Railway lifecycle and replay controls preserve matrix/color words, bounds and fallback behavior.\n\nThe earlier published 1904 phone scene on `ca22329c` passed cold loading, its complete driving route, walking into reach, trusted Stop and held-wheel checks. Its first-open Inspector timeout remains a nonpass. The later native Inspector component check on `e0f3b883` passed person hydration and trusted Find/Back; that is a component result, not a new 3D-world result.\n\nDraft while the latest DEV changes and fresh current-commit CI are resolved. Broad photographic appearance, gait, boarding, riding and natural seated animation remain open. This PR delivers incremental driving and interaction work.\n","labels":[]